TITLE:: RCSurface
summary:: A parametric surface in R^m, sampled for its tangent lines and rulings
categories:: Libraries>reCurrent
related:: Classes/RCLines, Classes/RCProjection

DESCRIPTION::
A surface is a Function (u, v) → Array of strong::dim:: numbers over uRange × vRange. link::Classes/RCLines#*projected:: samples it (link::#-grid::, link::#-random::, link::#-walk::), takes a tangent segment or the v-line (the ruling) through each sample and projects it on a score space with an link::Classes/RCProjection::. The presets are the surfaces Xenakis drew for Metastasis and the Philips Pavilion (ruled: the cone, the conoid, the hyperbolic paraboloid, the hyperboloid of one sheet), the surface ruled by two rails, the surface of the tangents of a curve, and closed surfaces for projected textures (sphere, torus, the Clifford torus in R^4). Rulings run along v where a preset is ruled.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: func
(u, v) → Array of dim numbers.
argument:: dim
argument:: uRange
argument:: vRange
argument:: du
argument:: dv
Partial derivatives, Functions (u, v) → Array; central differences (link::#-eps::) when nil.
argument:: name

subsection:: Presets
METHOD:: plane
code::[u, v, 0]::.
METHOD:: hyperbolicParaboloid
code::[u, v, u v / c]::, doubly ruled: the string section of Metastasis, the Pavilion's walls.
METHOD:: conoid
The right conoid (helicoid) code::[v cos u, v sin u, c u]::, rulings through the axis.
METHOD:: cone
code::[v cos u, v sin u, v]::: the fan.
METHOD:: cylinder
METHOD:: hyperboloid
One sheet, code::[cos u - v sin u, sin u + v cos u, v]::, the v-lines straight.
METHOD:: sphere
u the azimuth, v the elevation.
METHOD:: torus
argument:: bigR
argument:: r
METHOD:: clifford
The Clifford torus in R^4, code::[cos u, sin u, cos v, sin v] / sqrt 2::: flat, and every rotation of R^4 shows it differently to a projection.
METHOD:: rails
S(u, v) = A(u) + v (B(u) - A(u)) for two Functions u → Array: the strings between two rails.
METHOD:: tangentDevelopable
S(u, v) = C(u) + v C'(u) for a curve C (a Function u → Array): ruled by the tangents of the curve, the Xenakeur construction as a surface.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: at
The point at (u, v).
METHOD:: du
METHOD:: dv
The partial derivatives at (u, v).
METHOD:: tangent
code::cos(angle) * du + sin(angle) * dv::.
METHOD:: normal
The unit normal (dim 3 only), nil elsewhere or where the tangents are dependent.
METHOD:: grid
nu × nv samples code::[u, v]:: over the ranges, the ends included unless the parameter is periodic.
METHOD:: random
n samples uniform over the ranges, seeded.
METHOD:: walk
A random walk of n samples from strong::start:: (the ranges' middle by default), wrapped over a periodic range, clipped otherwise; seeded.
METHOD:: uPeriodic
METHOD:: vPeriodic
Whether a parameter wraps (set by the presets).
METHOD:: eps
The step of the central differences.
METHOD:: dim
METHOD:: uRange
METHOD:: vRange
METHOD:: name

EXAMPLES::
code::
~s = RCSurface.torus(2, 0.7);
~s.at(1, 2);
~s.normal(1, 2);
~s.grid(8, 4).size;   // 32
~s.walk(16, 0.3, 0.3, seed: 1);
::
